   "ruling": "Ruling: scope; i1040gi p. 14, Married Filing Separately; p. 15, Qualifying Surviving Spouse, \"1. Your spouse died in 2023 or 2024 and you didn't remarry before the end of 2025.\" A separate return is outside the tool: s3.mfs refuses scope.ready and the return's closing lines (executed on stage8.hoh.child.ctc with status mfs and household.married No: f1040.line31, line33 and line37 refused at s3.mfs), so an unmarried MFS filer gets no completed return. A remarried QSS filer fails household.qss_eligible, whose first test is the no-remarriage test, and household.qss_fails refuses line 12e (executed with status qss: line 12e and line 24 refused at household.qss_fails). The gate covers the two supported statuses that can contradict the marriage facts (single with a year-end marriage; joint with no year-end marriage and no 2025 death), as BUG-0286 records; its expression was not changed by the gate-wave rewrite. As the prior ruling. Project stands.",
   "subject_key": "96509bdea2a17e14eeac502a130b3a023c7a42d4744af6607658be62a03c5beb"
  }
